From a64f33f5c9ac8ed55a87d8c302f33038891ef2f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:24:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pm4: accept EVENT_WRITE_EOP INT_SEL=3 without raising an IRQ

PM4CmdEventWriteEop::SignalFence hits UNREACHABLE for
InterruptSelect::IrqUndocumented (INT_SEL=3), so a guest EOP with that
selector aborts the emulator right after the data write.

INT_SEL=3 is SEND_DATA_AFTER_WR_CONFIRM: the data write waits for write
confirmation and no interrupt is sent (Mesa RADV documents it as "Wait
for write confirmation before writing data, but don't send an
interrupt"). The data write is already performed above, so accept the
value as a no-IRQ case.

OpenGNM's sceGnmDrawCmdEventWriteEop uses INT_SEL=3 for every
non-discard label write, which made homebrew GNM workloads crash.
PM4CmdReleaseMem::SignalFence currently treats 3 like an IRQ; that may
be inaccurate too, but is left unchanged here.
---
 src/video_core/amdgpu/pm4_cmds.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/amdgpu/pm4_cmds.h b/src/video_core/amdgpu/pm4_cmds.h
index f4a0702..0c2d260 100644
--- a/src/video_core/amdgpu/pm4_cmds.h
+++ b/src/video_core/amdgpu/pm4_cmds.h
@@ -504,6 +504,11 @@ struct PM4CmdEventWriteEop {
             signal_irq();
             break;
         }
+        case InterruptSelect::IrqUndocumented: {
+            // INT_SEL=3 (SEND_DATA_AFTER_WR_CONFIRM): the data is written after
+            // write confirmation (done above) and no interrupt is sent.
+            break;
+        }
         default: {
             UNREACHABLE();
         }
